# Git LFS. The guide's screenshots and screen recordings are binary and get
# retaken, so every version git stores is a whole extra copy that can only be
# removed by rewriting history. Pointers keep the history light; the bytes live
# in LFS and are fetched only for the revision being checked out.
#
# History was rewritten once, over v0.25.0..main, to move the media already
# committed there into LFS as well. No tag moved and no release changed: every
# guide asset was added after v0.25.0, which is the last tag. That rewrite is
# not to be repeated - it was cheap only because the repository was private,
# unforked and had a single working copy.
#
# LFS hooks live in .husky/, not .git/hooks, because this repository sets
# core.hooksPath. See .husky/pre-push.
*.mp4 filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
apps/web/public/guide/*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
